From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: training's goalie goes out after the ball and back at a kickoff
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The TRAINING page (tweak patch 0095) can take the opponent's goalie out in
the middle of a match (tweak patch 0044 sends it far off the field, unseen
and with no collisions), and put it back. Put back at once, it would play
from up there, and its next save crashed (Goalie::InitActionSave, as the
ball came to the goal); taken out with the ball in its hands, the ball went
with it. A goalie holding the ball now stays until it lets go (a throw, a
pass), and one that went out stays out until the next kickoff, whose
Goalie::Reset puts it in its goal again, seen and solid (cCharacter::Reset).

diff --git a/src/Game/Goalie.cpp b/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
index 5a8f70b..fed0924 100644
--- a/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
@@ -234,6 +234,14 @@ inline void Goalie::InitGoalieActionData()
     }
 }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Port tweak "Training": whether each side's goalie is out of the match. It
+// goes out at once, but comes back only at a kickoff (Reset), which puts it in
+// its goal again: back in play from far off the field, its next save would
+// crash.
+static bool sTrainingGoalieOut[2];
+#endif
+
 Goalie::Goalie(eCharacterClass gcc, const int* pTemplate,
     cSHierarchy* pHierarchy, cAnimInventory* pAnimInventory,
     const CharacterPhysicsData* pPhysicsData, GoalieTweaks* pTweaks,
@@ -257,6 +265,11 @@ Goalie::Goalie(eCharacterClass gcc, const int* pTemplate,
     mFatigue.Reset();
     mFatigue.mfRecoverRate = pTweaks->fFatigueRecoverRate;
     m_pHeadTrack->m_bTrackOOI = true;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port tweak "Training": a new match's goalies start in.
+    sTrainingGoalieOut[0] = false;
+    sTrainingGoalieOut[1] = false;
+#endif
 }
 
 void Goalie::ResetAnimState()
@@ -301,6 +314,15 @@ void Goalie::Update(float dt)
     // match when the launcher says so: it touches neither the ball nor the
     // players, casts no shadow, is not drawn, and stands far from the field.
     if (GetTrainingSide() == 1 - m_pTeam->m_nSide && !mscharged_tweak_training_away_goalie())
+    {
+        // One holding the ball keeps it, and goes out once it lets go: out
+        // at once, the ball would leave with it.
+        if (g_pBall == 0 || g_pBall->m_pOwner != this)
+        {
+            sTrainingGoalieOut[m_pTeam->m_nSide] = true;
+        }
+    }
+    if (sTrainingGoalieOut[m_pTeam->m_nSide])
     {
         m_pPhysicsCharacter->m_CanCollideWithBall = false;
         m_pPhysicsCharacter->m_CanCollideWithCharacters = false;
@@ -4537,6 +4559,12 @@ void Goalie::Reset(const nlVector3& v3Position, unsigned short aDirection)
     mbNegGoalieNetCheck = false;
     mpLooseBallInfo = 0;
     RestoreBallAfterMegaStrike(false);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port tweak "Training": a kickoff brings a goalie that was out back
+    // (cCharacter::Reset makes it seen and solid again); Update takes it out
+    // again while the opponent still has none.
+    sTrainingGoalieOut[m_pTeam->m_nSide] = false;
+#endif
 }
 
 
